-- title:
--   From a patching datum to modularity at an explicit level
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a natural number (primality is not assumed) and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb Z$ with $\Delta(W)\neq 0$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal) with finite residue field, and suppose $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual representation over $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, i.e. a $2$-dimensional $k$-space with an action of the group of $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphisms of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ factoring through a finite extension, and let $\mathcal D$ be a predicate on $2$-dimensional adically continuous representations over local $\mathcal O$-algebras. The data consist of: (i) $D$, an inhabitant of the project's [`GaloisRep.DeformationRingData`](def/GaloisRep_DeformationRingData.html#L8), i.e. a local noetherian adically complete $\mathcal O$-algebra $R=D.R$ with local structure map whose residue field is generated by that of $\mathcal O$, absolute irreducibility of $\bar\rho$, a representation $D.\rho$ over $R$ satisfying $\mathcal D$ and residually equivalent to $\bar\rho$, together with the universal property that for every local noetherian adically complete $\mathcal O$-algebra $A$ with local structure map whose residue field is likewise generated by that of $\mathcal O$, and every $\rho_A$ over $A$ satisfying $\mathcal D$ and residually equivalent to $\bar\rho$, there is a unique $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi:R\to A$ admitting a proof of locality for which $\varphi_*D.\rho\simeq\rho_A$; (ii) a level $N\neq 0$, a finite set $S$ of primes containing every prime divisor of $N$, the hypothesis that the $\mathbb Z$-lattice of cusp forms of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ with integral $q$-coefficients spans the whole space over $\mathbb C$, a character $\theta$ of the $S$-anemic Hecke algebra $\mathbb T_S=\mathbb Z[T_\ell,U_q:\ell,q\notin S]$ with values in $k$, and a [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8) $H$ over a local noetherian adically complete $\mathcal O$-algebra $T$ that is finite and free over $\mathcal O$: a ring map $\pi:\mathbb T_S\to T$ whose reduction equals $\theta$ pushed along the induced map of residue fields, with $\mathcal O[\pi(\mathbb T_S)]=T$, with the residue field of $T$ generated by that of $\mathcal O$, with the property that every $\chi:\mathbb T_S\to\mathcal O$ whose reduction modulo $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ is $\theta$ factors through $\pi$ via an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $T\to\mathcal O$, and a representation $H.\rho$ over $T$ with residually absolutely irreducible reduction and $\det(X-H.\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell))=X^2-\pi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ for all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ and all Frobenius elements at $\ell$; (iii) a local $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi:R\to T$ with $\varphi_*D.\rho\simeq H.\rho$, a nontrivial module $M$ over both $R$ and $T$ on which $R$ acts through $\varphi$, and a Taylor–Wiles patching datum $P$ for $(\mathcal O,p,r,R,M)$ in the sense of [`Algebra.PatchingDatum`](def/Algebra_PatchingDatum.html#L39); (iv) a representation $\rho_W$ over $\mathcal O$ satisfying $\mathcal D$, residually equivalent to $\bar\rho$, with $\det(X-\rho_W(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell))=X^2-a_\ell(W)X+\ell$ for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid\Delta(W)$ and every Frobenius at $\ell$, where $a_\ell(W)=\ell+1-\#W(\mathbb F_\ell)$ computed from the reduction of the given model. The conclusion is that $W$ is a modular model of level $N'=N\cdot\prod_{q\in S,\,q\nmid N}q$: there is a normalised eigenform of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(N')$ (in the project's sense: first $q$-coefficient $1$, multiplicativity at coprime indices and the two prime-power recursions) whose $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient equals $a_\ell(W)$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid\Delta(W)$ and $\ell\nmid N'$.
--
--   This is the concluding assembly step of the Taylor–Wiles modularity lifting argument in Diamond's formulation: given the universal deformation ring, the Galois representation over the local Hecke algebra, a patching datum and a $p$-adic representation of the curve of the prescribed deformation type, one concludes modularity of the curve. Unlike the textbook statement, the conclusion names the level explicitly as $N$ multiplied only by those primes of $S$ not already dividing $N$ — so exponents of primes dividing $N$ are not raised — and asserts only an eigenform with matching $q$-coefficients at good primes away from that level, with no claim about conductors or newforms. It feeds the two modularity lifting theorems at conductor level for $p=3$ and $p=5$, where the explicit level keeps cube-freeness of the auxiliary level under control.
